---
import csv from './downloads/events.csv?raw';
const events=csv.trim().split('\n').slice(1).map(line=>{const [event_id,occurred_at,shop_id,endpoint]=line.split(',');return{event_id,occurred_at,shop_id:Number(shop_id),endpoint};});
const months=[{key:'09',name:'September',start:'1 Sep',end:'1 Oct'},{key:'10',name:'October',start:'1 Oct',end:'1 Nov'},{key:'11',name:'November',start:'1 Nov',end:'1 Dec'}];
---
<figure class="pruning" data-pruning data-events={JSON.stringify(events)} aria-labelledby="r12-pruning-title">
 <figcaption id="r12-pruning-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Which ranges can contain an answer?</figcaption>
 <label>Query <select data-query><option value="oct">October · direct time bounds</option><option value="cross">31 Oct to 2 Nov · direct bounds</option><option value="endpoint">Endpoint /catalogue · no time bound</option><option value="wrapped">October · UTC date expression</option></select></label>
 <p class="predicate" data-predicate data-live></p>
 <div class="partitions">{months.map(m=><div class="partition" data-month={m.key}><p class="panel-label">{m.name}</p><p class="bounds">[{m.start}, {m.end}) · UTC</p>{events.filter(e=>e.occurred_at.slice(5,7)===m.key).map(e=><div class="event" data-event={e.event_id}><strong>{e.event_id}</strong><span>{new Date(e.occurred_at).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{day:'numeric',month:'short',timeZone:'UTC'})}<br/>{e.occurred_at.slice(11,19)}Z</span><small>{e.endpoint}</small></div>)}<p data-verdict={m.key} data-live>Not checked yet</p></div>)}</div>
 <p data-answer data-live></p><p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 1 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>Read the pruning comparisons as text</summary><p>The direct October range can exclude September and November, returning E2 and E3 from October. The range from 31 October to 2 November must visit October and November, returning E3 and E4. Endpoint /catalogue supplies no time boundary, so all three partitions remain candidates; E1, E2 and E4 qualify. Applying a UTC date conversion to the key still returns E2 and E3, but the demonstrated PostgreSQL plan cannot use it to prune these time partitions.</p></details>
 <p class="caption">A conceptual pass over the four request-event rows supplied in the CSV. Outlined events qualify; “skip” marks a partition proved outside the direct range. The four native query shapes were checked separately on PostgreSQL 18.6. The drawing does not run SQL.</p>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pruning]').forEach(root=>{
 const events=JSON.parse(root.dataset.events!),select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-query]')!;const months=['09','10','11'];
 const candidates=()=>select.value==='oct'?['10']:select.value==='cross'?['10','11']:months;
 const matches=(e:any)=>select.value==='endpoint'?e.endpoint==='/catalogue':select.value==='cross'?e.occurred_at>='2026-10-31'&&e.occurred_at<'2026-11-02':e.occurred_at>='2026-10-01'&&e.occurred_at<'2026-11-01';
 const predicates={oct:'occurred_at >= 1 Oct AND occurred_at < 1 Nov',cross:'occurred_at >= 31 Oct AND occurred_at < 2 Nov',endpoint:"endpoint = '/catalogue'",wrapped:"(occurred_at AT TIME ZONE 'UTC')::date in October"};
 const draw=(s:number)=>{const c=candidates();root.querySelector('[data-predicate]')!.textContent=predicates[select.value];
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-month]').forEach(el=>{const checked=months.indexOf(el.dataset.month!)<s;el.classList.toggle('skipped',checked&&!c.includes(el.dataset.month!));el.querySelector('[data-verdict]')!.textContent=!checked?'Not checked yet':c.includes(el.dataset.month!)?'Read candidate partition':'Skip · outside query range';});
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-event]').forEach(el=>el.classList.toggle('qualifies',s===4&&matches(events.find(e=>e.event_id===el.dataset.event))));
 root.querySelector('[data-answer]')!.textContent=s===4?`Answer: ${events.filter(matches).map(e=>e.event_id).join(', ')}. Read ${c.length} of 3 candidate partitions.`:'Answer not read yet.';
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s===0?'First compare the query with each partition’s declared bounds. Row filtering comes afterwards.':s<4?(c.includes(months[s-1])?`${['September','October','November'][s-1]} cannot be excluded from this query. Its rows still need the predicate checked.`:`${['September','October','November'][s-1]} cannot contain a timestamp in the direct query range. Skip it without reading its rows.`):select.value==='wrapped'?'The converted date gives the right answer, but this key expression did not prune the native time partitions. Direct instant bounds make the range available.':'Read only candidate partitions, then test their rows. Pruning a partition and selecting rows inside it are separate jobs.';
 };
 const p=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw});select.addEventListener('change',()=>{p.render();root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();});
 });
</script>
<style>.pruning{padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.2rem var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.7rem}select{display:block;max-width:100%;font:inherit;padding:.5rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.predicate{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.8rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.partitions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.7rem}.partition{padding:.6rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);background:var(--color-surface)}.panel-label{font-weight:600;margin:.3rem 0}.bounds{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.event{padding:.5rem;margin:.6rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);display:grid;font-size:.82rem}.event small{overflow-wrap:anywhere;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.skipped{border-style:dashed}.skipped .event{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.qualifies{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:-2px}.controls{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}button{font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);padding:.45rem .65rem;cursor:pointer}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.5}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}[data-explanation]{min-height:4.5em;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem}[data-hold]{height:3px;width:100%;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;width:0;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent)}.caption{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin-top:1rem}summary{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:520px){.partitions{grid-template-columns:1fr}.event{grid-template-columns:2rem 1fr;gap:.5rem}.event small{grid-column:2}select{font-size:.8rem}}</style>
